-- Independent receipt archive (R2): import the 177 historical/orphaned PDFs from the manual
-- backfill (scripts/receipt-archive/) into archive metadata.
--
-- Gap this closes: 20261025110000_document_pdf_versioning.sql's backfill only sourced from
-- public.documents (the 516 currently-referenced PDFs) -- it never represented the 177
-- objects that exist in Storage/R2 but aren't any document's current pdf_url. Without this,
-- archive.backup_health would report them as "missing" immediately after deployment, even
-- though they were already uploaded to R2 and independently SHA-256 verified (source hash ==
-- manifest hash == R2 hash, zero mismatches) during the manual historical backfill.
--
-- Source of truth: scripts/receipt-archive/out/manifest.jsonl, the actual output of that
-- verified backfill run -- not re-derived from any live table (there's nothing to derive from;
-- these objects have no current document row by definition). The 516 referenced entries in that
-- same manifest are NOT re-imported here: they're already correctly covered by the previous
-- migration's backfill from public.documents.signature_hash, which is the identical sha256 for
-- the same unmodified bytes (confirmed during that same verification pass).
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT (storage_path) DO NOTHING, same guarantee as every other insert into
-- this table. Safe to apply to a database that has never seen these objects (inserts them) or
-- one that already has (no-ops).

